Keeps dashboard/public/ in git.

deploy/docker/Dockerfile.dashboard does an unconditional
`COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public`, so the Docker build FAILS outright
when this directory does not exist:

    failed to compute cache key: "/app/public": not found

Next.js does not create it, and it held no tracked files, so it existed only on
machines where someone had made it by hand. Every image so far was built on such
a machine; a clean clone could not build the dashboard at all.

It also could not survive a deploy: deploy/fleet/fleet.sh rsyncs `dashboard`
with --delete, so shipping from a tree without this directory would have removed
it from the node as well, breaking any later rebuild there too.
